{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"4a6bc49a56caf02d","type":"text","text":"# **Income Statement/ Profit and Loss**\n\nDefines **profit** or **loss** generated by a company during a given time period.\n\n* **Revenues**: the amount charged for delivery of products or services.\n* **Expenses**: the cost of using up company resources to earn revenues.\n\nProfit(loss) = Revenues - Expenses","x":-600,"y":-721,"width":660,"height":260},
		{"id":"e58dc1831a691ab5","type":"file","file":"Attachments/Pasted image 20260908110450.png","x":-1306,"y":-893,"width":560,"height":604},
		{"id":"b5e74bd71904cb1b","type":"text","text":"# **Kinds of Profit**\n\n### Gross profit\n\n* Revenues - Cost of sales\n(cost of sales is not the only cost incurred by a company)\n\n### Operating profit/income (EBIT)\n\nOperating income = Gross profit - other operating expenses\n\n(other operating expenses like marketing, utility costs, admin depreciation expenses etc.)\n\n*EBITDA is operating income before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortisation*\n\nEBITDA = EBIT (or operating income) + Depreciation + Amortisation\n(adds those depreciation and amortisation expenses back so its higher than EBIT)\n\n### Net Profit\n\nIf the company has borrowed money to finance its activities, it will have to pay interest. Deducting interest expense from operating income determines a companies profit before tax:\n\nEarnings before taxes = EBIT (or operating profit) - Interest expense\n\nIncome taxes owed by company on its earnings are then deducted to arrive at net income/profit or profit after tax:\n\nNet income = EBIT - Interest expense - tax expense.\n\nCompany shareholders are interested to know about income per share, called earnings per share (EPS) which is net income divided by number of shares outstanding and dividends per share.\n\nEBIT: Earnings before interest and taxes\nEBITDA: Earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortisation\n\n\n","x":-1026,"y":-200,"width":660,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"fa9d8d880dae5261","x":-1026,"y":-1240,"width":668,"height":261,"color":"6","type":"text","text":"# Profit Summaries\n\nGross Profit = Revenues - Cost of sales\n\nOperating income/profit (EBIT) = Gross profit - operating expenses\n\nEBITDA = EBIT + Depreciation expenses + amortisation expenses\n\nNet income = Operating income - interest expenses - tax expenses\n\n"}
	],
